(Conclusion) Tj T*
(This project successfully demonstrates the implementation of graph traversal algorithms) Tj T*
(using Recursive Depth First Search \(DFS\) and Breadth First Search \(BFS\). The program) Tj T*
(identifies all connected components in the graph, labels each vertex with the smallest) Tj T*
(vertex number in its connected component, performs deterministic DFS and BFS traversals, and) Tj T*
(reconstructs minimum-edge routes using the BFS parent array.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(By sorting adjacency lists before traversal, the output remains consistent and reproducible) Tj T*
(regardless of the order in which edges are provided. The project also highlights the) Tj T*
(practical use of graphs in representing campus walkways and emergency navigation systems.) Tj T*
(Overall, the implementation satisfies all the requirements specified in the problem) Tj T*
(statement while maintaining efficient time and space complexity) Tj T*
() Tj T*
